messages:
Harper N: Pushed a small docs PR to consolidate function-calling examples to the new structured-output schema. Focus: migration notes, a couple of edge-case examples, and tiny SDK accessor snippets. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4802 :wave:
Diego R: Can you paste the minimal example you used for the docs? Want to mirror it in the Go/TS snippets.
Harper N: Example in the PR:
```json
{"request_id":"req_9","toolOutput":{"choices":[{"id":"c1","score":0.92}],"meta":{"version":"v2"}},"confidence":0.92}
```
Maya Q: Two quick asks: 1) include a union case (choices[] OR {error:string}) 2) show parse-fallback when the tool emits malformed JSON (fallback to `raw_text`).
Diego R: For migration we should show a safe accessor for older clients:
```js
const out = res.toolOutput ?? res.tool_result;
```
Harper N: Added both. Union example I added:
```json
// either
{"choices":[{"id":"c1","score":0.8}]}
// or
{"error":"timeout"}
```
Maya Q: And the parse-fallback snippet I liked:
```ts
let parsed;
try { parsed = JSON.parse(body); }
catch { parsed = { raw_text: body }; }
const output = parsed.toolOutput ?? parsed.tool_result ?? parsed.raw_text;
```
docs-bot: lint OK for PR 4802.
link-checker: Link check failed -> https://docs.redwood.ai/specs/old-tool-schema (404)
Harper N: Thanks, replacing with canonical: https://docs.redwood.ai/schemas/structured-output-2025.json and pushed the fix.
Diego R: Under Guardrails section recommend required routing fields: `request_id` (string) and `confidence` (0..1 float). Mention they are recommended for routing tools but optional for others. Also add `example_response` for typegen consumers.
Maya Q: Small runtime check: confirm `confidence` is 0..1 float. I'll ask eng-runtime and link the confirmation in the PR comments.
Harper N: Done, eng-runtime confirmed 0..1 float and I added the note. I'll wait for one docs review and then merge. If anyone wants to drop additional edge-case examples (nullable arrays, empty-choices), add them here and I'll fold them in. :pray:
